MACHINE OF RECORD FAILURE LOG
Study: ray-distributed-lab. Date: 2026-11-08 (America/Toronto).
Machine: the Muse VM named in PREREGISTRATION.md as frozen
(4 cores, 7.7 GB RAM, Python 3.12.3). Outcome: Ray cannot start
on this machine. No measured study run had taken place when
this was established; the only prior executions were 1-epoch
smoke runs of arms A and B to /tmp, which are not study data.
This file is the preserved evidence behind Amendment A1 to
PREREGISTRATION.md and DECISIONS.md D1.

1. Arm C smoke (Ray Train, TorchTrainer), 2026-11-08 about
   21:25 EST, wall time 13m58s, ended in failure:
     ray.exceptions.RpcError: Timed out while waiting for GCS
     to become available.
   (raised from ray._raylet.GcsClient / InnerGcsClient.
   standalone). The GCS server process itself started and kept
   printing periodic stats for the whole attempt; no raylet
   logs were ever produced.

2. Minimal ray.init probe with _node_ip_address="127.0.0.1":
   same hang; the driver never returned from init.

3. Minimal gRPC probe (grpcio, a Ray dependency), in-process
   server and client on 127.0.0.1, default poll strategy
   (epoll1): the call never completed; grpc deadline exceeded
   after 10 s.

4. Same probe with GRPC_POLL_STRATEGY=epoll:
     E1108 ... ev_posix.cc:134] No event engine could be
     initialized from epoll
   epoll is not available in this sandbox.

5. Same probe, separate server and client processes, both
   GRPC_POLL_STRATEGY=poll: DEADLINE_EXCEEDED again.

6. Same probe, in-process, GRPC_POLL_STRATEGY=poll:
   UNAVAILABLE: failed to connect to all addresses; last
   error: UNAVAILABLE: ipv4:127.0.0.1:<port>: recvmsg:
   Connection reset by peer (104).

Conclusion: gRPC does not function on this VM under any poll
strategy tried. Ray 2.60 requires gRPC for its GCS and raylet
control plane, so no Ray arm (C, or R in either pattern) can
run here. Plain PyTorch (arms A, B) and the plain inference
loop (arm P) do run here, but splitting arms across machines
would void the within-study comparisons every hypothesis
depends on, so the whole study moves. Precedent in this
programme: kafka-streaming-lab made the same move for the
same class of reason (its Amendment A1, 2026-11-08).

Successor machine (verified before the amendment was written):
BlackBoxV2, Jesun's always-on Ubuntu machine: 8 cores, 14 GB
RAM, 135 GB free disk, Python 3.14.4, x86_64. Ray 2.60.0 and
torch 2.15.0 both publish cp314 wheels.
